00:24:37.640 --> 00:24:38.720
Covering up job.

00:24:39.990 --> 00:24:45.190
Perfect.

00:24:45.610 --> 00:24:46.890
And no one's the wiser.

00:24:48.980 --> 00:24:50.680
Flamingo, what are you looking at?

00:24:51.440 --> 00:24:52.300
Read my lips, pal.

00:24:52.810 --> 00:24:54.580
You didn't see anything.

00:24:55.960 --> 00:24:57.400
He understands.

00:25:01.370 --> 00:25:03.010
I had gazed on him while unfinished.

00:25:03.520 --> 00:25:04.420
He was ugly then.

00:25:04.710 --> 00:25:07.390
But when those muscles and joints were rendered capable of motion,

00:25:07.750 --> 00:25:10.410
it became a thing such as even Dante could not have conceived.

00:25:11.040 --> 00:25:11.750
A writer.

00:25:12.290 --> 00:25:14.690
Mary Shelley creates a chilling yet sympathetic character.

00:25:15.190 --> 00:25:18.790
Her rich power of description allows her readers and our makeup artist

00:25:18.790 --> 00:25:20.490
to unleash their imaginations.

00:25:20.850 --> 00:25:26.660
We were thinking, do we do a space age, kind of a robotic type of monster?

00:25:27.210 --> 00:25:30.000
But then we decided that we wanted to keep the Frankenstein

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.570
monster, very

00:25:31.570 --> 00:25:33.790
human, to

00:25:33.790 --> 00:25:36.470
create a sense of

00:25:36.470 --> 00:25:37.950
pity for this

00:25:37.950 --> 00:25:39.990
character, but still with the horror

00:25:39.990 --> 00:25:42.170
involved in piecing

00:25:42.170 --> 00:25:44.030
together this creation.

00:25:44.860 --> 00:25:46.580
Here's the actor who plays Frankenstein's

00:25:46.580 --> 00:25:47.850
creature. As you'll see,

00:25:48.150 --> 00:25:49.890
makeup is going to do wonders for him.

00:25:50.250 --> 00:25:52.220
The first thing

00:25:52.220 --> 00:25:54.240
is to create the

00:25:54.240 --> 00:25:56.030
scars, a little bit

00:25:56.030 --> 00:25:58.350
jagged so that they would look rather rough.

00:25:58.350 --> 00:26:00.000
The whole process

00:26:00.030 --> 00:26:01.590
will take a while, but that's okay.

00:26:01.850 --> 00:26:03.990
It'll give the actor time to envision the character

00:26:03.990 --> 00:26:04.890
he's about to become.

00:26:06.240 --> 00:26:08.310
Icing on the cake was this

00:26:08.310 --> 00:26:10.210
contact lens that totally

00:26:10.210 --> 00:26:12.470
blotted out the color of

00:26:12.470 --> 00:26:16.430
his eye. But how was I terrified

00:26:16.430 --> 00:26:18.210
when I viewed myself in a transparent

00:26:18.210 --> 00:26:20.030
pool? His watery eyes

00:26:20.030 --> 00:26:22.170
seemed almost of the same color as the

00:26:22.170 --> 00:26:23.870
dumb white sockets in which they were set.

00:26:24.710 --> 00:26:26.540
I am sorry.

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:28.410
A great book, a little makeup,

00:26:28.410 --> 00:26:30.000
and a lot of imagination.

00:26:30.480 --> 00:26:34.070
The recipe for Frankenstein's bone-chilling and sympathetic creature.
